<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">

  <PropertyGroup>
    <TargetFrameworks>net48;netstandard2.0;netstandard2.1;net8.0</TargetFrameworks>
    <IsPackable>true</IsPackable>
    <Description>The synchronous traversal contracts for Copse (ITreenumerator, ITreenumerable and its dimension-split parents) plus the walker tier (TreeWalker, TreeWalkerResult, ITreeTopology, IWalkableTreenumerable) and the traversal vocabulary both families speak (NodePosition, NodeVisit, NodeTraversalStrategies, Option, ...). The dependency root: references nothing.</Description>
  </PropertyGroup>

  <!-- No InternalsVisibleTo (2026-08-15): the seal lives at the SUBSTRATE boundary, not
       here: TreeWalker.Topology is public (the vantage's bound-physics half; a topology
       navigates relative to any handle, a walker relative to its focus; the signatures
       carry the frame), and what stays hidden is the STORE behind each topology
       (implementations sealed, accessors internal, wholesale views read-only). The
       operator tier and third parties hold identical access. -->

</Project>
